    "id": "bead-abacus",
    "name": "Bead Abacus",
    "description": "A big counting frame on a clean bright tabletop in soft daylight: warm hardwood posts and rails, polished steel rods and chunky lacquered wooden beads (round, bicone or disc) in a small confident palette with paint worn to bare wood on the rims. Quantities become physical and countable: beads slide along their rods as a pushed block and clack home with a tiny settle; rows are labelled bars, shares, counts or place values; desk nameplates at the row ends update when the beads land; a 10x10 frame fills for percentages, and ten beads return while one moves on for a carry.",
